Your Majesty,

It is my duty, however unwelcome, to note that certain reformist books have b=
een seen in the Queen's apartments, and that Her Majesty debates points of re=
ligion more freely than is perhaps seemly.

I raise it only that Your Majesty may judge.

Your servant,
S. Gardiner
